		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">23</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">1. To find out 3rd angle, we figured out the following logic
    a. Calculate the sum of given 2 angles
    b. Subtract it from 180. The result will be the 3rd angle.
2. To read input, we use readLine(). But it will always give a string. 
3. But string operations are different from arithmetic operations (e.g. 5+5 will give 10, but "5"+"5" will give "55")
So, how can we do the calculations? Luckily, Javascript has a way to convert string to integer.</attribute>
